# CQ-16 · affordance
#
# Question: Which entities offer an affordance, and which one?
# Persona:  P3 — director / creative technologist. Whether a prop can be held,
#           worn or ridden is a staging fact, and it is the fourth axis of the
#           trait bundle rather than a free-text attribute.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §5.4 (`vso:affordance`); §5.12 (closed to five values)
# Form:     SELECT — one row per entity per affordance
# Note:     `vso:affordance` is multi-valued (§5.12: no `sh:maxCount`, because
#           a thing can be both Holdable and Edible), so the entity column may
#           repeat. Only the hand-authored canonical scene uses the axis; the
#           gallery does not, which this answer says plainly.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?doc ?entity ?affordance ?class
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?entity vso:affordance ?affordance .
    OPTIONAL { ?entity vso:class ?class }
  }
}
ORDER BY ?doc ?entity ?affordance
